       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I was wrong to offer earlier to enter it with a confirmation note.\n\nThe total is 9,600 mg/day, three times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication that calls for it. Sustained dosing at that level carries a high risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and normal baseline kidney and liver function doesn't change that. Entering it would put a likely-harmful order into the system.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Up to 800 mg PO every 6 hours (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf there's a clinical reason for exceeding the maximum, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy first. If you think I've misread the order, for example if you meant 2,400 mg total per day, tell me and I'll enter it that way."
